{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Like</b> — Rabbi Moses said: this refers to [the phrase] 'and the utterances will hear,' for we all die. And in my opinion: the meaning is that they fled from David's men, after the manner of 'and all my bones shall be scattered' (Psalms 22:18)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 141, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:26.887296966Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}